   Setup — this machine's logins and terminal

   kit welcome --checks --machine   ⧉   ▶️ 
   kit ran it once, as this screen opened; the checks below are what it found.
   ⧉ copies it, to run in your own shell, and ▶️ runs it again here.

   ❌ gh is not logged in to github.com
      gh auth login --hostname github.com · it needs you at the keyboard
   ❌ kit check finds 2 differences from the release
      read: kit help check

   This step checks what the work on this machine needs. It checks the
   command-line tool of the code forge kit reaches, GitHub's gh, and your login
   there. In a terminal, it also judges the terminal kit runs in, and names
   each of its settings that makes kittui slower or worse.

   When a check fails, the line under it gives the command that fixes it, or
   says where to read more. Run the command yourself, or have kit run it and
